hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1102","Chapter on watchwords in war, 1141 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Ahmasi narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufrah, from one who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If the enemy attacks you by night, your watchword is: Ha-Mim, they shall not be helped."
